hello and welcome to my latest monthly  leaders briefing you're joining me here  from eckington leisure centre in the  swimming pool which i'm sure many of you  aware is currently closed but for a very  very good reason we're currently  undergoing some major works to refurbish  and realign the pool and as well as  introduce a number of carbon climate  change initiatives like solar panels on  the roof and air source heat pumps which  we hope will make the pool warmer and  make the whole facility much more carbon  friendly and actually probably one of  the most carbon friendly in the whole  area this is really exciting time for  the council and it's projects like this  that we're doing around the district  that are helping us to  meet our climate change commitments  moving on to another piece of sad news  we've recently learned of the death of  one of our former councillors peter  ramshaw who served the ashov award  for many years with with great service  to  his residents and that community and our  thoughts and prayers and condolences are  very much with his family at this this  difficult time and we want to say a big  thank you  for all of peter's work over the years  and then another really sad event that  has gripped the nation is the incredibly  sad death of sir david amos mp uh in in  hugely tragic circumstances  again our thoughts and prayers are with  his family and all of his colleagues at  this extremely difficult time  you know the murder of a public servant  doing his job and representing his  people is an incredibly awful thing to  have happened and it must make us ask  questions about all of our  collective safety but it's vital that we  as public servants and politicians and  and council officers continue to be open  uh facing to the public and engage with  the public  and so we don't want to to change too  much or put up any barriers or walls  from residents accessing our services or  accessing their local councils so we  want to continue to do those engagement  events but we will have to be mindful of  public safety moving forward  one of those recent events was our meet  the council where we we we held two  events one in eckington here and one  down in  clay cross and these events were all  about showing our residents about the  services that we provide as a district  council and giving residents the  opportunity to ask me and some of my  cabinet colleagues fellow councillors  questions about what the council's doing  to address the issues that they care  about and that's a really important  manifesto commitment for us we we pledge  to be a listening council so doing those  events is a great way to be able to talk  to our residents and find out about the  issues that they've been facing and give  them the opportunity to to raise issues  with us as their  local councillors we've also recently  done a national customer service week  event at our offices at mill lane where  we invited residents to come in and talk  to us about some of the services we  provide right from our council base and  then recently we also did  our armed forces event celebration in  drumfield where  we had a number of members of the  different armed forces community come  and and and talk to residents about some  of the uh the things that they do  we had some fantastic vehicles on site  in the car park next to the leisure  center and we had an excellent uh trade  and  market uh stall event in the in the  leisure centre itself as well as a  church service to commemorate the work  that our  fantastic armed forces community do for  us  so moving on we've also recently  introduced a new policy  for for licensing for taxi drivers and  private hire vehicles we've introduced  mandatory cctv which is in line with the  the new government guidance around  licensing and we're really proud to be  one of the first councils in davashi to  have done this we feel it will help make  our residents and the drivers themselves  feel more safe and more comfortable  when when using those services we're  also going to be working with  neighbouring district councils and  authorities up in south yorkshire to  encourage them to also  adopt the policy  and and that will make it much better  for the whole region to have that policy  in place  we also wanted to remind everyone that  earlier this year we launched a british  sign language video interpreter service  at our council offices and our leisure  centres and that's to help make the uh  the council services more accessible to  the deaf community so we want to remind  everyone and hope that those members of  the deaf community will be able to use  that when they come and visit us at our  leisure centres or council offices  in other news we've also  relaunched our community action grants  for the next round of our action grant  scheme so that's for grants for  community groups for up to 500 pounds  and that's to help  different groups around the district to  be able to tackle some of the local  issues or or support local events within  their area so please do get in touch and  apply for one of the grants if you feel  it might be useful in your community  we've also launched again our eco  schools grant scheme  this is for grants for up to 500 pounds  for secondary schools and up to 250  pounds for primary schools and it's to  support our students to be able to carry  out projects that are supporting the the  climate change mission that we all have  it's really exciting project and we'd  encourage all of our schools to apply  now we've also been working across the  county with other district councils and  the county council to set up what's  known as vision derbyshire now this is a  project that's all about ensuring that  the different tiers of councils  collaborate much better on projects that  affect the whole county and one of the  schemes that vision derbish has recently  set up is a business support scheme now  this is a this is to offer any  businesses around the county as free  support and advice but we're also  offering as part of that scheme grants  of up to  ten thousand pounds to eligible  businesses so if you're a business owner  yourself uh please do look it up and  find out more information about it and  if you're eligible please do apply for  the grants because they're there to  support you particularly as we as we  recover from covered so finally thank  you everyone for for watching today  please do keep stay tuned to our website  and our social media accounts for all  the latest news i hope you found the  updates today useful  and hopefully you'll look forward to  joining us here  back at eckington pool  hopefully around christmas time when we  reopen  to the public and it will look  absolutely fantastic i can assure you so  look forward to seeing you then and  thank you very much  you
 

